      "source": [
        "# Lecture 5.1. Radon Measure\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Radon Measures on $\\mathbb{R}$\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {#def-borel-radon-measure}\n",
        "## Borel and Radon Measures\n",
        "If $\\Omega$ is a topological space, any measure defined on the Borel $\\sigma$-algebra $\\mathcal{B}(\\Omega)$ is called a **Borel measure**. \n",
        "\n",
        "A Borel measure $\\mu$ on $\\mathbb{R}$ is called a **Radon measure** if it assigns finite measure to all bounded intervals:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\mu((a, b]) < \\infty \\quad \\text{for all } -\\infty < a < b < \\infty.\n",
        "$${#eq-radon-finite-intervals}\n",
        "\n",
        "*(More generally, a Radon measure on a Hausdorff topological space is a locally finite Borel measure that is inner regular with respect to compact sets; on $\\mathbb{R}$, this simplifies to finiteness on compact sets $\\mu(K) < \\infty$.)*\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Stieltjes Premeasures and Correspondence\n",
        "\n",
        "Recall that for any non-decreasing, right-continuous function $F: \\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}$, the associated Stieltjes set function $\\mu_F((a, b]) = F(b) - F(a)$ defines a premeasure on the algebra of finite disjoint unions of half-open intervals $\\mathcal{A}_{\\mathbb{R}}$.\n",
        "\n",
        "The next result shows that every Radon measure on $\\mathbb{R}$ arises from a unique (up to an additive constant) Stieltjes premeasure.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {#thm-radon-measure-characterization}\n",
        "## Characterization of Radon Measures on $\\mathbb{R}$\n",
        "If $\\mu$ is a Radon measure on $\\mathbb{R}$, then there exists a non-decreasing, right-continuous function $F: \\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}$ (unique up to an additive constant) such that:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\mu((a, b]) = F(b) - F(a) \\quad \\text{for all } -\\infty < a \\le b < \\infty.\n",
        "$${#eq-radon-f-correspondence}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.proof}\n",
        "## Proof of @thm-radon-measure-characterization\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Uniqueness:**\n",
        "   If $G: \\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}$ is another non-decreasing right-continuous function satisfying $\\mu((a, b]) = G(b) - G(a)$, then for all $a, b \\in \\mathbb{R}$:\n",
        "   $$G(b) - G(a) = F(b) - F(a) \\implies G(b) = F(b) + [G(0) - F(0)].$$\n",
        "\n",
        "   Setting $C = G(0) - F(0)$, we have $G(x) = F(x) + C$, establishing uniqueness up to a constant $C \\in \\mathbb{R}$.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **Existence:**\n",
        "   Define $F: \\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}$ centered at $0$ by:\n",
        "   $$\n",
        "   F(x) := \n",
        "   \\begin{cases}   \n",
        "    \\mu((0, x]), & x \\ge 0, \\\\    \n",
        "    -\\mu((x, 0]), & x < 0.    \n",
        "    \\end{cases}\n",
        "   $${#eq-f-construction-centered}\n",
        "\n",
        "   * **Interval Measure Identity:** For any $a < b$, set additive subtraction yields $\\mu((a, b]) = F(b) - F(a)$.\n",
        "   * **Monotonicity:** For $x \\le y$, set inclusion $(0, x] \\subseteq (0, y]$ (or $(y, 0] \\subseteq (x, 0]$ for negative values) together with monotonicity of $\\mu$ implies $F(x) \\le F(y)$.\n",
        "   * **Right-Continuity:** Fix $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$ and let $x_n \\downarrow x$ with $x_n > x$. Then $(x, x_1] \\setminus (x_n, x_1] = (x, x_n] \\downarrow \\emptyset$. By continuity of measure from above for finite measure sets:\n",
        "     $$\n",
        "     F(x_n) - F(x) = \\mu((x, x_n]) \\xrightarrow{n \\to \\infty} 0.\n",
        "     $$\n",
        "\n",
        "     Thus, $F(x) = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} F(x_n)$, proving right-continuity.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Premeasure Continuity Equivalences\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {#prp-premeasure-continuity-equivalences}\n",
        "## Equivalences for Premeasures (Driver, Prop. 6.3)\n",
        "Let $\\mu$ be a finitely additive set function on an algebra $\\mathcal{A}$. The following conditions are equivalent:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. $\\mu$ is a premeasure (countably additive) on $\\mathcal{A}$.\n",
        "2. **Monotone Increasing Continuity:** If $\\{A_n\\}_{n=1}^\\infty \\subseteq \\mathcal{A}$ with $A_n \\uparrow A \\in \\mathcal{A}$, then $\\mu(A_n) \\uparrow \\mu(A)$ as $n \\to \\infty$.\n",
        "\n",
        "Moreover, if $\\mu(\\Omega) < \\infty$, these are also equivalent to:\n",
        "\n",
        "3. **Monotone Decreasing Continuity:** If $\\{A_n\\}_{n=1}^\\infty \\subseteq \\mathcal{A}$ with $A_n \\downarrow A \\in \\mathcal{A}$, then $\\mu(A_n) \\downarrow \\mu(A)$ as $n \\to \\infty$.\n",
        "4. **Continuity at Empty Set from Above:** If $\\{A_n\\}_{n=1}^\\infty \\subseteq \\mathcal{A}$ with $A_n \\downarrow \\emptyset$, then $\\mu(A_n) \\downarrow 0$.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.proof}\n",
        "## Proof of @prp-premeasure-continuity-equivalences \n",
        "\n",
        "* **(1) $\\Rightarrow$ (2):** Let $A_n \\uparrow A \\in \\mathcal{A}$. Set $B_1 = A_1$ and $B_n = A_n \\setminus A_{n-1} \\in \\mathcal{A}$ for $n \\ge 2$. The sequence $\\{B_n\\}_{n=1}^\\infty$ is pairwise disjoint with $\\bigcup_{n=1}^\\infty B_n = A$ and $\\bigcup_{n=1}^N B_n = A_N$. By countable additivity:\n",
        "  $$\n",
        "  \\mu(A) = \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\mu(B_n) = \\lim_{N \\to \\infty} \\sum_{n=1}^N \\mu(B_n) = \\lim_{N \\to \\infty} \\mu(A_N).\n",
        "  $$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "* **(2) $\\Rightarrow$ (1):** Let $\\{B_n\\}_{n=1}^\\infty \\subseteq \\mathcal{A}$ be pairwise disjoint with $\\bigcup_{n=1}^\\infty B_n = B \\in \\mathcal{A}$. Define $A_N := \\bigcup_{n=1}^N B_n \\in \\mathcal{A}$. Then $A_N \\uparrow B$. Applying (2):\n",
        "  $$\n",
        "  \\mu(B) = \\lim_{N \\to \\infty} \\mu(A_N) = \\lim_{N \\to \\infty} \\sum_{n=1}^N \\mu(B_n) = \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\mu(B_n).\n",
        "  $$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Equivalence of (3)–(4) for Finite Measures:** Follows directly by complementary set subtraction: $\\mu(B \\setminus A) = \\mu(B) - \\mu(A)$ whenever $A \\subseteq B$ and $\\mu(B) < \\infty$. \n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Cumulative Distribution Functions (CDFs)\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {#def-borel-cdf}\n",
        "## Cumulative Distribution Function\n",
        "Let $\\mu$ be a Borel probability measure on $\\mathbb{R}$ (so $\\mu(\\mathbb{R}) = 1$). The **Cumulative Distribution Function (CDF)** of $\\mu$ is the function $F_\\mu: \\mathbb{R} \\to [0, 1]$ defined by:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "F_\\mu(x) := \\mu((-\\infty, x]).\n",
        "$${#eq-cdf-def}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {#cor-cdf-characterization}\n",
        "## Characterization of Probability CDFs\n",
        "A function $F: \\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}$ is the CDF of a unique Borel probability measure $\\mu$ on $\\mathbb{R}$ if and only if it satisfies:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Monotonicity:** $F$ is non-decreasing;\n",
        "2. **Right-Continuity:** $F(x^+) = \\lim_{y \\downarrow x} F(y) = F(x)$ for all $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$;\n",
        "3. **Asymptotic Limits:**\n",
        "   $$\n",
        "   \\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} F(x) = 0 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\lim_{x \\to +\\infty} F(x) = 1.\n",
        "   $${#eq-cdf-limits}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Classification of Borel Probability Measures on $\\mathbb{R}$\n",
        "\n",
        "Every CDF $F$ can be decomposed into three standard types of behavior: Absolutely Continuous, Purely Discrete, and Singular Continuous.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Absolutely Continuous Measures\n",
        "A measure $\\mu$ is continuous/absolutely continuous if $F_\\mu$ is continuous everywhere. In this case, singletons have zero measure:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\mu(\\{x_0\\}) = \\lim_{x \\uparrow x_0} \\mu((x, x_0]) = \\lim_{x \\uparrow x_0} (F_\\mu(x_0) - F_\\mu(x)) = 0.\n",
        "$${#eq-singleton-zero-measure}\n",
        "\n",
        "*Example (Uniform Distribution):*\n",
        "$$\n",
        "F(x) = \\begin{cases}  0, & x \\le 0, \\\\ x, & 0 \\le x \\le 1, \\\\ 1, & x \\ge 1. \\end{cases}\n",
        "$${#eq-uniform-cdf-example}\n",
        "\n",
        "In the following, we use Python to visualize the CDF of the uniform distribution on $[0, 1]$."
      ],
