        "### Purely Discrete / Point Mass Measures\n",
        "A measure $\\mu$ is purely discrete if its CDF $F_\\mu$ is a step function supported on a countable set of point masses $\\{x_k\\}$.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Example (Discrete Jump Measure):*\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\mu = \\frac{1}{3}\\delta_0 + \\frac{1}{9}\\delta_1 + \\frac{5}{9}\\delta_2.\n",
        "$${#eq-discrete-measure-example}\n",
        "\n",
        "Note that the CDF $F_\\mu$ is discontinuous at the points $x_0 = 0$, $x_1 = 1$, and $x_2 = 2$, with jump sizes equal to the corresponding point masses:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "F_\\mu(x) = \n",
        "\\begin{cases}  \n",
        "0, & x < 0, \\\\ \n",
        "1/3, & 0 \\le x < 1, \\\\ \n",
        "4/9, & 1 \\le x < 2, \\\\ \n",
        "1, & x \\ge 2. \n",
        "\\end{cases}\n",
        "$${#eq-discrete-cdf-jump}\n",
        "\n",
        "In the following, we use Python to visualize the CDF of this discrete measure."
      ],
      "id": "902ac3b0"
